@title  PCSE00120 - New Game: title screen, difficulty, opening movie, the Velvet Room, name entry
@game   PCSE00120
@shot-every 1000

# WHAT THIS RECIPE PROVES
# ----------------------
# The title boots, reaches its title screen, starts a NEW GAME at NORMAL difficulty, plays
# its two front-end movies, reaches the Velvet Room (Igor's dialogue), enters a name, and
# goes on into the opening cutscene movie. Every screen along the way renders through the
# recompiler (no fixed-function fallback), the title music and confirm sounds play, and the
# movies decode.
#
# THE ONE THING THAT COSTS A SESSION IF IT IS NOT WRITTEN DOWN: this title sits on a BLACK
# screen forever with no input, looking perfectly healthy while it does. Every press below
# is held 8 frames; the guest samples the pad once a display frame.
#
# WHERE THE SCREENS ARE (measured, shot every 200-400 frames):
#   f2000  the boot notices (Vox Populi / PSN prompt) - a cross dismisses each
#   f2400  the P4G logo splash, then the CRIWARE splash
#   f3200  the yellow title screen; f3400 "PRESS ANY BUTTON"
#   f3790  the main menu: NEW GAME / CONFIG / LOAD GAME / TV LISTINGS, NEW GAME selected
#   f4400  the pre-game notices again, then the difficulty select (NORMAL preselected)
#   f5900  "Start at NORMAL difficulty? Yes/No" - cross takes Yes
#   f6500  "We hope you have fun with the game" text box, then the disclaimer
#   f6900  the first movie (the truck in the fog), ~1,500 frames
#   f8700  the opening anime movie (Margaret, Igor) - plays to the Velvet Room
#   f14000 the Velvet Room: Igor's "guest with an intriguing destiny" dialogue
#   f15700 name entry: the last name is filled with the preselected letter, START ends it
#   f17900 the first name, START ends it, cross confirms "Proceed? Yes"
#   f18100 Igor's tarot reading, then the scene fades to the intro cutscene movie
#   f24000 the intro cutscene (the beach, the news desk, the train)
#
# WHAT IS NOT RIGHT YET, and where the evidence is (working-area/agent-notes.md):
#   - the Velvet Room's 3D backdrop composites BLACK behind the portraits; its draws replay
#     to the right velvet blue in a capsule, so the loss is in a later draw of the frame.
#   - the movies' sound depends on the stream-info fix of 2026-09-01c.
#
# THE PRESSES ARE A MASH THROUGH THE NOTICES, NOT A MINIMAL SEQUENCE. Which single press
# first leaves each notice has not been bisected; `explore` over 300..900 is how.

